---
import { DOCS_PATH } from "../../site.config.ts";
// Plain <details>: no script, keyboard and screen reader support come from the browser.
---

<section id="faq" class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="faq-title" class="section__title">Questions</h2>

    <div class="faq">
      <details class="faq__item">
        <summary>Does 0Crypto hold my money?</summary>
        <div class="faq__answer">
          <p>
            No. 0Crypto is software that runs in your own Cloudflare account, and nobody else operates it. In watch mode,
            payments land in your wallet and the Worker cannot spend them. In routed mode, the keys live in your Worker,
            which only you control.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq__item">
        <summary>Do I need a terminal?</summary>
        <div class="faq__answer">
          <p>
            Watch mode: no. You deploy, sign in and connect your wallet in the browser. Routed mode: yes, for setup. It
            needs a seed phrase, a contract deployment on each EVM chain you enable, funded hot wallets and API keys, and the docs
            walk you through each step.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq__item">
        <summary>What does it cost?</summary>
        <div class="faq__answer">
          <p>
            Cloudflare's Workers Paid plan, billed to you by Cloudflare. There is no 0Crypto fee and no cut of your
            payments. Network fees still apply when coins move on-chain, and routed mode also pays gas for sweeps (EVM
            chains and Solana), rented energy on Tron, and the swap or shield fees of privacy routing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq__item">
        <summary>What if I lose my passkey?</summary>
        <div class="faq__answer">
          <p>
            On the sign-in page, choose “Lost your passkey or moved to a new domain?”. It asks for a fresh code from your
            Worker's logs, the same way as the first setup, lets you create a new passkey, and signs every device out.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq__item">
        <summary>Can I use my own domain?</summary>
        <div class="faq__answer">
          <p>
            Yes. Add the domain to the Worker in Cloudflare. Passkeys belong to one domain, so sign in once more on the new
            domain with “Lost your passkey or moved to a new domain?”. <a href={`${DOCS_PATH}custom-domain/`}
              >How to add a domain</a
            >.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq__item">
        <summary>Is it legal for me?</summary>
        <div class="faq__answer">
          <p>
            Run 0Crypto for your own business only. Accepting money on behalf of other merchants makes you a custodian,
            which falls under money transmitter rules (for example MSB in the US) or crypto-asset service provider rules
            (MiCA in the EU). There is no multi-merchant mode, by design. Get advice for your own jurisdiction.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq__item">
        <summary>Why does the Deploy button fail?</summary>
        <div class="faq__answer">
          <p>
            Cloudflare's Deploy button can only copy a public GitHub repository. While the repository it points at is
            private, Cloudflare stops with an error. You can still <a href={`${DOCS_PATH}deploy/#deploy-by-hand-developers`}>deploy by hand</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
